window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"zac","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Skill","Zac","Zac"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Survive this window: Q into E is two 10s cooldowns and lands before your blobs stabilise you - hug tower, concede CS, and never fight on his timer."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Passive blobs sustain you back to even - absorb his poke, deny the Determination stacks that arm his revive, and let the clock run."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Grim Deliverance (R) is a damage-and-heal, not a peel, and 110s - but your R roams better than it duels: a mid-lane gank converts your losing lane into a winning game."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Tank stats plus blob sustain out-last his poke - but keep Grievous Wounds up, because his Q and R both heal him back."}],"wants":{"you":["A quiet early lane conceded without deaths","Blobs that blank his poke and stack math","Tank items turning his damage into noise"],"foe":["The level-2 Q-E all-in before blobs land","Darkin Glaive chip that arms his revive","A snowball started before your item spike"]},"early":"Level 1 is even farming - you are a famously weak early laner but nothing he has yet punishes that. Level 2 is his window: The Darkin Glaive (Q) into Aureate Rush (E) is two 10s cooldowns and it beats a blob-less Zac, so hug tower, give up contested CS, and reach 3 healthy where blobs even it back out.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are a patience contest that suits you fine: absorb poke, collect every blob, and deny the Determination stacks that arm his revive. At 6 his Grim Deliverance heals him through your damage while your R roams better than it duels - so shove and bounce mid or bot, because your map game beats winning this lane straight.","late":"Your first tank item flips the lane for good: blob sustain out-lasts his poke and his kill script needs windows that no longer exist. Two items in you are simply ahead - W Unstable Matter's percent-HP damage chews his bruiser frame and a charged E into R engage wins any fight he takes, with anti-heal up.","whys":["Level 1 is even - both of you farm, and nothing punishes your weak early game yet.","He owns level 2: Q into E, both on 10s, punishes you before blobs land.","Level 3 evens out as you start sustaining off passive blobs.","Levels 4-5 stay even as you farm up and play safe.","Level 6 evens out - his R is a 110s damage-heal, not the peel it looks like.","First item is yours: tank stats and blob sustain out-last his poke.","Two items in your percent-HP damage and E-R engage keep you well ahead."]});
